# Context root for the three frontend Dockerfiles is the repository root, not the app
# directory — see any of frontend-web/Dockerfile, frontend-app/Dockerfile or
# frontend-admin/Dockerfile's header comment for why. Everything here is either
# irrelevant to a Next.js build (backend/, ops/) or regenerated inside the image anyway
# (node_modules, .next) — none of it needs to cross the daemon boundary before the first
# instruction even runs.

node_modules
**/node_modules

.git

# The backend has its own Dockerfile and its own build context; nothing here is a
# dependency of a Next.js build, and backend/ carries Gradle caches large enough to slow
# the context upload down for no reason.
backend/

# Deployment configuration and, more importantly, the one place secrets almost live —
# ops/.env is git-ignored but not docker-ignored by default, and a frontend image has no
# use for any of it.
ops/

# Regenerated by each build stage; shipping a stale one from the host would either be
# wasted bytes or, worse, silently used instead of what CI just built.
.next
**/.next

# Test tooling output — never a build input, always safe to leave behind.
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
blob-report
.playwright

.cursor/
.idea/
.github/
